{"utc": "2026-09-24T15:34:49Z", "version": "V6.0", "event": "rejected", "stage": "PROBE", "reason": "g->N main effect 0.027 << 0.10 (3 dev seeds). Exact: f = cos(th)(cos(phi)cos(chi) u + sin(phi)sin(chi) u^3) + sin(th) sin(phi-chi) u^2; u^3 = 0.6 P1 + 0.4 P3, so at g=1 the P1 part carries ~91% of the variance (N ~ 0.03). Also sin(phi-chi) shrinks as chi -> phi, so the P2 content of the Q write peaks at intermediate g (C2: HL 0.195 > HH 0.176). Parametric processor fault, fixable by design: chi_max < 0 cancels P1 at g=1 and makes sin(phi-chi) grow with g."}
